{
  "formId": "IRD04.QF.004",
  "formTitle": "Consolidated General Application Form (CGAF) for Extension of Stay of Temporary Visitor's Visa",
  "documentType": "application_request",
  "availability": "active",
  "checkoutEligible": null,
  "checkoutEligibleNote": "Not yet decided -- same open business-classification question as the other mapped forms. This mapping covers field-level automation only; checkout eligibility is a separate business decision.",
  "reproductionRightsVerified": true,
  "reproductionRightsNote": "Confirmed directly on the form itself: 'This document may be reproduced and is NOT for sale.', printed at the top of the page.",
  "pageWidthPt": 612,
  "pageHeightPt": 936,
  "sourcePdf": "original.pdf",
  "derivedFrom": "Measured from a 300 DPI raster of the real original PDF (downloaded from the private fis-bi-forms-library R2 bucket, originals/IRD04.QF.004.pdf), a Microsoft Word export with a standard (0,0)-origin MediaBox (no offset correction needed, unlike ARD04.QF.003). Every date field (Date of Birth, three 'Date of Validity' fields, Date of Latest Arrival) is drawn as THREE SEPARATE single-line boxes -- one each for DD / MMM / YYYY, with a plain dash character printed between them -- not a per-character comb grid like every other previously-mapped form's date fields; confirmed by direct visual inspection before measuring (a first assumption of a comb grid was discarded once the real boxes were seen). All checkboxes on this form are small (~7.3pt square) Word/Wingdings-glyph checkboxes, visually and dimensionally consistent across every group measured.",
  "measurementNotes": {
    "dateFieldsAreThreeBoxesNotCombs": "Unlike every other mapped form, this form's DD-MMM-YYYY date fields (dobDay/Month/Year, dateValidity1/2/3 Day/Month/Year, dateLatestArrival Day/Month/Year) are each THREE INDEPENDENT single-line free-text boxes (one full box per Day, Month, Year) with a plain printed dash between them, not a comb grid of individual character cells. Each is therefore mapped as an ordinary freeTextFields entry (e.g. dobDay holds the whole 'DD' value as one string, not split into per-character cells), confirmed via direct visual crop before measuring any coordinates.",
    "reasonForExtensionSevenLines": "The 'State your reason for extension of stay' field prints SEVEN ruled lines (six full-width lines plus one shorter 7th continuation line sharing its row with the staff-only evaluator box) -- mapped as seven independent freeTextFields (reasonLine1-7), each its own question, with reasonLine1 required and reasonLine2-7 required:false (the applicant fills only as many lines as needed), the same established pattern already used by 2014-08-015's multi-line purpose/documents fields.",
    "evaluatorFieldStaffOnly": "'Name and signature of evaluator/assessor' (in its own bordered box to the right of reasonLine7) is BI-staff-only -- never auto-filled, consistent with every other form's wet-ink/staff-determination field policy; marked suppliedBy:staff, visibleTo:staff, and optional in staffFieldRequirements.",
    "photoRequirementNotEmbedded": "The form's photo box (top-left, '2x2 inch colored photograph, white background, permanent glue, taken within the past 3 months') is a physical photo attachment requirement, not a fillable field -- it is NOT mapped as a coordinate field and is NOT embedded into the generated PDF by this automation. It is handled entirely through the existing supporting-document-upload feature of the customer wizard, the same way every other form's physical-attachment requirement (e.g. passport copy, ID copy) already is.",
    "consentParagraphNotPopulated": "The Data-Privacy-Act consent paragraph's two inline blanks ('I, ___, personally or through my agent/representative ___') are wet-ink declaration elements, deliberately left blank by this automation -- same policy as every other mapped form. Only the signatureBlock's dateLine and signatureLine coordinates (measured via direct pixel scan, since -- unlike the reason lines above -- these bottom lines are drawn as vector graphics, not printed underscore characters) are recorded, never auto-filled.",
    "methodOfApplicationAndModeNotGated": "Method of Application (Personal/Authorized Representative) and Mode of Application (Regular/Express) are mapped as two independent single-select checkboxSelect groups, same pattern as every other multi-option checkbox group on this form. nameOfAuthorizedRep/biAccreditationNumber are mapped as ordinary (always-askable) freeTextFields rather than conditionally gated on methodOfApplication=AuthorizedRepresentative, consistent with how every other form's conditionally-relevant field (e.g. spouse name, parent/guardian name) is handled elsewhere in this engine: always present as an optional question, answered 'N/A' when not applicable, per the form's own explicit 'write N/A if not applicable' instruction."
  },
